# Declared in-tree test artifacts.
#
# THE RULE: a test writes to "$BATS_TEST_TMPDIR" (bats) or mktemp -d. It may
# write inside the repo ONLY if the exact path is declared here.
#
# Paths are globs, relative to the repo root. tools/test-tree-guard.sh:
#   - sweeps these before every suite run, healing a tree left dirty by a run
#     that died before teardown (SIGKILL runs no teardown, and no trap helps);
#   - fails the suite on any created/modified path NOT listed here.
#
# Adding a line is a deliberate, reviewable exception. Prefer fixing the test.
#
# Why this file exists: a leaked fixture from a crashed run broke three
# subsequent runs in one day and baited a kill of a live suite, because the
# debris was indistinguishable from a real failure.

# tools/harsh-review.sh is a monolithic repo-wide script with no function-level
# test seam -- CHECK 8b-2 can only be exercised by placing a real file under a
# real skills/**/reviewers/ directory and running the whole script.
